1
00:00:03.478 --> 00:00:08.897
A lease with a rent review clause reminds
you in the Inbox a month before the notice

2
00:00:08.897 --> 00:00:10.397
deadline.

3
00:00:10.397 --> 00:00:14.739
It shows the review date, today's rent and
the new one, and when the notice must go

4
00:00:14.739 --> 00:00:16.239
out.

5
00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:20.510
Review increase opens the tenant's rent
review: the lease's terms, the next

6
00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.618
review, and the deadline for notice.

7
00:00:23.743 --> 00:00:29.243
The new rent is worked out from the lease
— 5% a year here — and you can adjust it.

8
00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:34.566
It starts on the review date. If the
deadline has already passed, it moves to

9
00:00:34.566 --> 00:00:37.355
the first month with full notice — never
backdated.

10
00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:44.330
Scheduled. Invoices from that month bill
the new rent, and the tenant's rent

11
00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.170
switches by itself on the day.

12
00:00:47.293 --> 00:00:51.863
Download the notice letter to print, or
email it — the PDF goes with it and the

13
00:00:51.863 --> 00:00:54.293
email is logged on the tenant's Comms tab.

14
00:00:57.206 --> 00:01:01.811
The terms are set on the tenant: a
percentage or a fixed amount, how often,

15
00:01:01.811 --> 00:01:04.206
the first review and the notice period.

16
00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:09.842
Skipping a review? Record no increase, and
the next reminder is for the following

17
00:01:09.842 --> 00:01:11.342
year.

18
00:01:11.342 --> 00:01:14.134
That's rent increases: reminded,
scheduled, notified — and never missed.
